---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const description =
  'Impeccable in sssf: the deterministic detect gate, the agentic design pass, and how to opt in.';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Design quality"
  description={description}
  current="/docs/design-quality"
  prev={{ href: '/docs/sandbox', label: 'Sandboxed runs' }}
  next={{ href: '/docs/quality-checks', label: 'Quality checks' }}
>
  <p>
    Design quality is enforced twice: a deterministic gate (<code>impeccable detect</code>, 59
    rules, no LLM) and an agentic pass (a <code>designer</code> agent running the impeccable
    skill). The agent proposes, the gate disposes.
  </p>

  <h2>The deterministic gate</h2>
  <p>
    <code>impeccable detect &lt;surface&gt;</code> ships configured by default as the
    <code>design</code> quality check. It exits 0 on a clean scan and 2 on hard anti-patterns —
    so the gate is pass/fail exactly like every other check. One advisory is a known false
    positive: the em-dash saturation rule counts <code>--</code> in CLI flags (e.g.
    <code>--adw-id</code>); it is advisory-only and never fails the gate. Per-project rule
    control lives in <code>.impeccable/config.json</code> (ignoreRules / ignoreFiles /
    ignoreValues) — committed, so the sandbox honors it.
  </p>

  <h2>The agentic pass</h2>
  <p>
    <code>sssf run sdlc_full "..."</code> runs the standard simple-sdlc chain with the
    designer in the middle: build → <code>design</code> (the designer runs the impeccable
    audit → critique → polish → optimize pass on the declared surface) → quality gates →
    review → commit. Two design-context phases are conditional: <code>init</code> (documenter
    runs <code>/impeccable init</code> → PRODUCT.md, once per project) and
    <code>document_design</code> (<code>/impeccable document</code> → DESIGN.md, when the
    design world changed). The deterministic gates — including <code>design</code> — verify the
    designer's work before anything commits.
  </p>

  <h2>Opting in (per project)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Run <code>sssf init --design-quality &lt;surface&gt;</code> — it declares the surface
        once (default <code>site/dist</code>) and wires the <code>design</code> check + the
        designer's scope to it.</li>
    <li>Run the full flow with <code>sssf run sdlc_full "..."</code> (or keep simple_sdlc — the
        gate still runs in any chain's quality loop).</li>
    <li>Per-project rule control: <code>.impeccable/config.json</code> ignores; advisory
        findings never fail the gate.</li>
    <li>Rebuild the runner image after any Dockerfile change — stale images keep failing the
        gates with exit 127.</li>
    <li>Full field reference: <a href="/docs/quality-checks">Quality checks</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
